<block><txt break.before="1">An Act to refer certain financial matters arising
out of the breakdown of de facto relationships to the Parliament of the
Commonwealth for the purposes of section 51 (xxxvii) of the <legref
jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="no">Constitution of
the Commonwealth</name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>
</content>


<content type="body">

<level type="clause" id="sec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_df5fefae-e470-4aba-aa36-02edf992b697"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_198bef00-f815-4b10-aa14-7bc1687e62c6"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name of Act and purpose</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.1-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ac55a2e3-3f45-4d8e-b393-ffe93ffdd5ef"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act is the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown" refid="act-2003-049"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Commonwealth
Powers (De Facto Relationships) Act
2003</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.1-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b98d0f60-a96a-45dd-b694-8f799140b1ce"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The purpose of this Act is to refer certain
financial matters arising out of the breakdown of de facto relationships to
the Parliament of the Commonwealth for the purposes of section 51 (xxxvii) of
the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="no">Constitution of the
Commonwealth</name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_92bdb13c-f1e5-4bb5-a647-3d446be983da"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_dcd6830e-f885-4082-b8a2-2e77e8ff1126"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act commences on a day to be appointed by
proclamation published in the Gazette.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_70accb16-c764-4231-a250-5601f7b4ddb2"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_afab2790-4820-4c17-b0cb-dd24e81b36ac"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_df8c90b9-39b8-4c02-ad21-56a66c92864d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_c9c3f1bb-b423-4a24-87ff-a53f293bfa1b"
id="sec.3-def.defactopartner"><b><i>de facto partner</i></b></defterm> means a
person who lives or has lived in a de facto relationship.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_ce5cbadc-0a18-4049-8239-76c29e5a9d62"
id="sec.3-def.defactorelationship"><b><i>de facto
relationship</i></b></defterm> means a marriage-like relationship (other than
a legal marriage) between two persons.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_e9ce64cd-d4ad-4894-bedc-d5a5c0516f2b"
id="sec.3-def.financialmatters"><b><i>financial matters</i></b></defterm>, in
relation to de facto partners, means any or all of the following
matters:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_9c24ca2d-45a6-4647-b4c3-7ba3c47adfd3" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the maintenance of de facto
partners,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8ca09e9b-06cf-43b8-a22f-2add91a88dad" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the distribution of the property of de facto
partners,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8bc86bb9-953f-4074-8423-607c104d198e" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the distribution of any other financial resources
of de facto partners, including prospective superannuation entitlements or
other valuable benefits of or relating to de facto
partners.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_00740e7e-1d54-47dc-a60b-e20e5a6919b6"
id="sec.3-def.property"><b><i>property</i></b></defterm> means any legal or
equitable estate or interest (whether present or future and whether vested or
contingent) in real or personal property of any description and wherever
situated, including money or choses in action.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9e28211d-6dfc-4aa3-bebe-03a0ddedef23"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">For the purposes of this Act, a de facto
relationship exists even if a de facto partner is legally married to someone
else or is in another de facto relationship.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_24331742-25c9-4a3a-84bf-a093334a93d6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A reference in this Act:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_fcc86e2d-e468-4c5c-a323-5506e2e11d43" id="sec.3-ssec.3-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to the property or other financial resources of
de facto partners includes a reference to the property or other financial
resources of either or both of them, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_da8e0d82-3d6d-49f9-af4d-a7e7d0775ee6" id="sec.3-ssec.3-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to the distribution of any such property or
resources includes a reference to the conferral of rights or obligations in
relation to the property or resources.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_449e00c5-a81e-4d80-bcc1-8abe8b171f30"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act extends to de facto relationships that
ended before the commencement of this Act.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_629d07ce-5cfb-4eeb-9126-7a5db4fcd91d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_a6a1fa7e-e12f-4d55-be49-ad97ed5460ef"
id="sec.4-he"><b>References</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7acd8bae-5f7e-4b08-a242-ae093f085079"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The following matters, to the extent to which
they are not otherwise included in the legislative powers of the Parliament of
the Commonwealth, are referred to the Parliament of the Commonwealth for a
period commencing on the day on which this Act commences and ending on the day
fixed, pursuant to section 5, as the day on which the references under this
Act are to terminate, but no longer:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_1b359e2a-d380-4081-a747-d35213aa11d7" id="sec.4-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">financial matters relating to de facto partners
arising out of the breakdown (other than by reason of death) of de facto
relationships between persons of different sexes,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8f1532bb-a404-466e-9eac-84f6e60d8b91" id="sec.4-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">financial matters relating to de facto partners
arising out of the breakdown (other than by reason of death) of de facto
relationships between persons of the same sex.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_fb2d3754-4b71-4d50-b5d2-b44b13240711"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The operation of each paragraph of subsection (1)
is not affected by the other paragraph.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_100f83bf-904d-4e14-83d3-7b4e832567e4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_9a5eabac-a658-4623-82a7-1a5d5c60055e"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Termination of references</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a71cec62-8ebf-4cef-b2d7-6431371fb9de"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may, at any time, by proclamation
published on the NSW legislation website, fix a day as the day on which the
references under this Act are to terminate.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e5918961-10ed-4ebd-9a1e-2f82b25f172a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The day fixed under subsection (1) must be no
earlier than the first day after the end of the period of 3 months beginning
with the day on which the proclamation is published under that
subsection.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_74d07844-fc31-4f39-af6f-03388ba18e69"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may, by proclamation published on
the NSW legislation website, revoke a proclamation published under subsection
(1), in which case the revoked proclamation is taken (for the purposes of
section 4) never to have been published.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1bbc28c7-5d1f-4603-a65b-abe3252bd931"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A revoking proclamation has effect only if
published before the day fixed under subsection (1).</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_351acf2d-9512-432b-b5ff-2f467baf4921"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(5)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The revocation of a proclamation published under
subsection (1) does not prevent publication of a further proclamation under
that subsection.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 5:</b> Am 2009 No 106,
Sch 3.9.</txt></content>
</level>
</content>


